      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-01-22_WidnesExaminer_art0040" n="art0040">
        <head>PROV. G.M. W. E. CLARE.</head>
        <p>PROV. G.M. W. E. CLARE.</p>
        <p>year, whilst the Deputy Grand Master of the district, he was also the President of the Dis- tact Widows' and Orphans' Fund. In January, 1911, Bro. Clare was appointed the secretary of his, lodge on the resignation of P.G. Henry Fogg, and still retains that offite Ile was also one of the representatives of the Warrington District to the Oddfellows' A.M.C., held at Scar- borough, in Whit-week, 1913. Bro. Clare has acted for tht past four years as the secretary for the District Bowling Com- mittee in connection with the Sir Gilbert Greenall Challenge Cup.</p>
