      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-01-22_WidnesExaminer_art0151" n="art0151">
        <p>night we had to go through with rations for about a mile and we had not•a bit of cover. The enemy swept the field with shells, because they knew that was the only way we could get through. They kept it up all the next day, and we had a terrible time of it."</p>
        <p>Private Rylands, who is 33 years of age, en- listed in February of last year. He had pre- viously been employed by Messrs. Joseph Cros- field and Sons, Ltd.. for which works' football team he formerly played. He is the possessor of several medals for his ability in this re- spect. He also belonged to the works' ambu- lance for about five years. As a boy he attended the Holy Trinity Day School.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-01-22_WidnesExaminer_art0152" n="art0152">
        <gap reason="ocrQuality" quantity="1" unit="words">
