      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-01-22_WidnesExaminer_art0201" n="art0201">
        <head>Four Men Killed And One Injured.</head>
        <p>Four Men Killed And One Injured.</p>
        <p>An explosion at Bedford, on Tuesday after- noon, resulted in the death of loir men and injury to a fifth. John Wildman, married, a time-expired sapper of the local Engineers, who returned home a month ago, was sawing with a hackshaw a shell which he had brought from the Front, not knowing there was a fuse in it, when it exploded. He was, killed instantly, as also were Donald Francis,George Trueman (aged 16), and Arthur Farrington (17). Herbert Papworth, married, was injured.</p>
        <p>CAUTION : Aak for "Owbridge" and take no substitute.</p>
