        <p>LIVERPOOL WINTER ASSIZES, JAN., 1916. The Commissions for holding thesetAssizes will be OPENED at LIVERPOOL on MONDAY, the 24th January. The Court will sit on Tuesday, the 25th January, at 11 o'clock a.m., and on every other day during the Assizes at 10.30 o'clock a.m., unless otherwise directed. The Prosecutors and Witnesses in the after- mentioned sloes are required to be in attendance at the timdrapecified on the following List, and. not earlier; and on all subsequent days, at the sitting of the Court; and the Trials are to pro- oeed in the order in which the Cases are arranged in the List, unless the Court shall otherwise direct, viz. On TUESDAY, the 25th January, at 11 O'clock a.m. The King versus Richard English, criminal assault; Richard Grundy, wounding; Michael dward Fitzgerald, bigamy; Beatrice Gamble and another, procuration; Mary Elizabeth Mor- gan, bigamy; Arthur Barton Ewing, larceny of a postal packet; Chan Chun Lee, attempted bribery; Ellen Robinson, concealment of birth; Thomas Bell, criminal assault; William Delaney, criminal assault; Thomas James Tabron, larteny of a postal packet; Max Kil- nlanovitch, receiving; Thomas Foster, man- slaughter ; Margaret Owens, bigamy; James Stanley Thorpe, larceny; And all Other Cases. „ All Indictments settled by Counstl must be rorwarded to me Engrossed and Abstracted. „ The foregoing Regulations will be strictly en- forced, and persons making default in the observance of them will be liable to have their costs disallowed. HERBERT STEPHEN, , Clerk of Assize. Office of Clerk of Assize, Preston, 19th January, 1916. wAll Depositions in cases for trial, together ith Recognisances and inunisitions, must be forwarded IMMEDIATELY to me at Preston.</p>
