        <p>THE EXAMINER, SATURDAY, JANUARY 22, 1916. SUCCESS IN THE POULTRY FRIENDLY SOCIETIES. YARD. BRO. WILLIAM E. CLARE, Pros'. Grand Master Of The Warrington District, 1.0.0., Manchester Unity. Bro. Clare, the newly-elected Grand Master of the Warrington District of the Manchester Unity for the current year has since his initia- tion in the Loyal "Haven of Rest" Lodge on the 16th October, 1899, fulfilled almost every office in his lodge and in the district: On his being elected as the N.G. of his lodge in 1903, Bro. Clare was the youngest member of that lodge to take such office, and from that time has been a district auditor and has served on various district and lodge committees. Last</p>
